    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-82" id="fn-82" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Purchased Power and Fuel Adjustment Clause (PPFAC) ratemaking treatment.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-83" id="fn-83" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Ancillary service purchases are charged based on coincident peak values, measured in MW. The units reported are the average of the monthly coincident peak for each customer, added together.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-84" id="fn-84" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Ancillary service purchases are charged based on coincident peak values, measured in MW. The units reported are the average of the monthly coincident peak for each customer, added together.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-85" id="fn-85" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Ancillary service purchases are charged based on coincident peak values, measured in MW. The units reported are the average of the monthly coincident peak for each customer, added together.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-86" id="fn-86" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <span xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Amount reflects losses that are settled financially.</span>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-87" id="fn-87" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">In December 2014, UNS Electric, Inc. (UNS Electric) and Tucson Electric Power (TEP), affiliated subsidiaries of UNS Energy Corporation, completed the purchase of Gila River Unit 3. TEP jointly owns 75% of Gila River Unit 3 with UNS Electric, the remaining 25% owner.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-88" id="fn-88" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Salt River Project Agricultural Improvement and Power District (SRP) is the plant operator on behalf of UNS Electric and TEP. Workforce operating the Gila River Unit 3 is primarily provided by SRP.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-89" id="fn-89" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Installed Capacity is measured in alternating current (AC).</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-90" id="fn-90" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:100.000%">
          <tr>
            <td style="width:1.0%"/>
            <td style="width:50.388%"/>
            <td style="width:0.1%"/>
            <td style="width:1.0%"/>
            <td style="width:23.155%"/>
            <td style="width:0.1%"/>
            <td style="width:1.0%"/>
            <td style="width:23.157%"/>
            <td style="width:0.1%"/>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom">
              <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Jointly-Owned Step-Up Transformer</span>
            </td>
            <td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom">
              <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Co-Owner(s)</span>
            </td>
            <td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom">
              <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">UNS Electric
                <br/>Ownership
              </span>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr style="height:26pt">
            <td colspan="3" style="border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:0 1pt"/>
            <td colspan="3" style="border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:0 1pt"/>
            <td colspan="3" style="border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:0 1pt"/>
          </tr>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">For the jointly-owned substations included in this report, some equipment is co-owned with UNS Electric, Inc. (UNS Electric) at various ownership percentages. Each party is charged its respective share of O&amp;M based on the ownership percentages and recorded to its functional FERC operations and maintenance account.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span>
          <br/>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">The facilities listed on pages 426-427 is not an exhaustive list of Substations and Switchyards at which UNS Electric is an owner of facilities recorded to Accounts E352, E353, E361 and E362. Substations and Switchyards in which UNS Electric is not an owner or majority owner, and for which it is not the operating agent, are excluded from this report. The Substations and Switchyards excluded are as follows:</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span>
          <br/>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Gila River</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Parker Dam Substation</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-91" id="fn-91" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">UNS Electric receives corporate cost allocations from UNS Energy Corp. Such costs are assigned based on the weighted average of three factors: assets, payroll, and revenues.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span>
          <br/>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">UNS Electric receives certain administrative services (finance, accounting, tax services, information technology, etc.) from Tucson Electric Power. Such costs are directly assigned where possible. Common costs are allocated on a cost-causative basis. UNS Electric and UNS Gas also bill each other for certain administrative and common costs. Amounts are based on the cost of services performed. Excluded from this page are "convenience" payments made to vendors by one entity on behalf of another and charged to the other affiliated entities.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span>
          <br/>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Management believes that the charges for the services are reasonable and appropriate.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span>
          <br/>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">All billings received from affiliated entities are charged to the same accounts that would have been charged for similar billings received from a non-affiliated entity.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
